# Environment variables for the sc Heerenveen Fansite.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the repository root and fill in the values. Git ignores .env, but not this file, so never
# put a real value here.
#
# Every variable that the site or the importer reads is listed below, with a line on what it's for. When you add one,
# add it here too, and to the app's schema for parseEnv (from @fansite/shared/env), which checks them at startup.

# Which environment the site runs in: local, acceptance or production. Only production may appear in search engines; the
# others send a noindex header and a robots.txt that refuses everything. The site doesn't start without it.
SITE_ENV=local

# The MariaDB database, as mysql://user:password@host:port/database. The site reads the source register from it, runs the
# migrations on it when it starts, and doesn't start without it. With SITE_ENV=acceptance it also puts the sources from the
# seed in. The value below is for the database that `docker compose up -d --wait` starts on your own computer: it has no
# password and only listens on that computer. The tests make their own database on this server, so the user must be
# allowed to create databases.
DATABASE_URL=mysql://root@127.0.0.1:3306/fansite

# The branch that `pnpm review` shows in the tab of the site and in the sidebar of Storybook. That command sets it for the
# dev servers it starts; you never set it yourself. Only `next dev` and `storybook dev` show it, so acceptance, production
# and the Storybook on GitHub Pages never do, whatever this holds.
# REVIEW_BRANCH=
